       <h1>AI Music Maker Suno Launches Spoken Word Generation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Suno</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Music</span> <span>#Speech Generation</span></div>
       <p>Suno, known for its AI music generation, is expanding its capabilities by introducing a new feature that creates spoken voices. This development marks a significant branch out from its original focus purely on music.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/ai-music-maker-suno-launches-spoken-word-generation.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The new functionality allows users to generate spoken voices using either provided scripts or prompted descriptions. This speech generation feature is currently accessible in public beta across Suno's web and mobile platforms, making it widely available.</p><p>A key aspect of this update is the ability to simultaneously generate voiceovers alongside background music. This integration offers a comprehensive solution for creating audio content that combines both spoken words and musical accompaniment.</p><p>What to watch: User adoption and further feature expansions from Suno.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article clearly explains the new feature and its availability based on the provided text.</p>
