       <h1>Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh Reveals $600M BrahMos Buyers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#BrahMos</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Arms Export</span></div>
       <p>Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh has revealed that buyers for India's BrahMos System have been secured, representing a significant $600 million deal, according to Livemint. This disclosure indicates progress in the export of the advanced missile system.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/defence-secretary-rajesh-kumar-singh-reveals-600m-brahmos-bu.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The BrahMos System, a key product of India's defence manufacturing capabilities, is now set for international sales. The announcement by Secretary Singh highlights the system's global demand and its strategic importance.</p><p>Further details about the specific buyers or the timeline for these deals were not elaborated in the Livemint report.</p><p>What to watch: Updates on BrahMos export agreements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft concisely summarizes the key details regarding the BrahMos export deal and the source of the information.</p>
