       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-03 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Dhaval Patel Warns Indian Students on US Master's Costs, H-1B Challenges</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#US Education</span> <span>#Master's Degree</span> <span>#Indian Students</span> <span>#H-1B Visa</span></div>
       <p>Indian students considering a master's degree in the United States face significant financial outlays, with costs estimated at $100,000. Dhaval Patel has issued a warning to these students regarding potential challenges in the job market and with H-1B visas, according to The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/dhaval-patel-warns-indian-students-on-us-masters-costs-h-1b-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Patel's cautionary advice highlights the need for prospective students to carefully consider post-graduation employment prospects and the complexities associated with securing an H-1B visa. The high cost of education combined with these hurdles presents a substantial concern.</p><p>The report from The Times of India underscores the importance of a realistic understanding of the full scope of pursuing higher education abroad beyond just admission.</p><p>What to watch: Further analysis on international student employment trends.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report effectively captures the core warning and the specific financial figure provided in the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
