       <h1>Education Ministry Unveils Rs 5.4 Crore Innovation Challenge</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education Ministry</span> <span>#Innovation</span> <span>#Challenge</span> <span>#Funding</span></div>
       <p>The Education Ministry has announced a new challenge encouraging individuals with innovative ideas to apply, according to a report by India Today. The initiative offers a substantial fund of Rs 5.4 crore to support promising concepts.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/education-ministry-unveils-rs-54-crore-innovation-challenge.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This program aims to stimulate creativity and provide financial backing for impactful projects within the education sector. The report from India Today highlights the opportunity for innovators to bring their ideas forward.</p><p>Further details regarding specific eligibility requirements, official application links, or submission deadlines were not specified in the summary.</p><p>What to watch: Upcoming announcements for application details.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the limited source material provided without inventing details or padding significantly.</p>
