       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-03 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Flydubai Captain Hailed for Composure After Mid-Air Stabbing</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Captain Smit Machchhar is being praised for his leadership after a co-pilot allegedly stabbed him during a September 30, 2026, Flydubai flight from Dubai to Tel Aviv. Despite the aircraft plummeting 17,400 feet, the injured captain maintained order by urging panicked passengers to refrain from retaliation and focus on stabilizing the plane.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/flydubai-captain-hailed-for-composure-after-mid-air-stabbing.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The flight was successfully diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, where all 174 passengers landed safely. Captain Machchhar, who suffered serious injuries, underwent emergency surgery before being airlifted to Abu Dhabi. Indian Ambassador Deepak Mittal confirmed the captain is stable and recovering well.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately synthesizes the mid-air incident and the captain's actions without adding extraneous information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
