     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-03 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Claims Asian Games Women's Hockey Gold, Ends 44-Year Wait</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sports</span> <span>#Hockey</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>India defeated China 1-0 in the Asian Games 2026 women's hockey final in Aichi-Nagoya, securing the nation's 16th gold medal at the Games. This victory marks India's first gold in women's hockey at the Asiad since 1982, ending a 44-year wait. The Indian side, led by captain Salima Tete, overcame World No. 4 China in a tightly contested match.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/india-claims-asian-games-womens-hockey-gold-ends-44-year-wai.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Lalremsiami Hmarzote, playing her 200th game for India, scored the decisive goal in the 10th minute of the first quarter. India maintained their 1-0 lead into half-time. A critical moment occurred in the second quarter when veteran Indian goalkeeper Savita Punia made an incredible save from a penalty stroke awarded to China, a moment described by NDTV Sports as gold-defining. In the third quarter, a penalty stroke for China was overturned after a referral, leading to a penalty corner from which Salima Tete made a crucial block.</p><p>India defended resolutely throughout the final two quarters to protect their lead, even as China substituted their goalkeeper for an outfielder in the final quarter in a bid for an all-out attack. The team secured direct qualification for the 2028 Olympics in Los Angeles with this win. This achievement caps a memorable year for Indian women's hockey, which also saw the team achieve its best-ever Women's Hockey World Cup finish earlier this year, coming fifth.</p><p>Throughout the Asian Games, India demonstrated dominance, securing seven wins in seven matches, scoring 69 goals, and conceding only three. This remarkable performance underscores a golden year for Indian women's hockey, culminating in the historic gold medal victory.</p><p>What to watch: India's preparations for the 2028 Los Angeles Olympics will now begin.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
