     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-03 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Irani Cup 2026: Rest of India Lead by 265 Runs After Day 3</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Irani Cup</span> <span>#Jammu &amp; Kashmir</span> <span>#Rest of India</span></div>
       <p>Rest of India has established a commanding lead of 265 runs by the close of Day 3 in the Irani Cup 2026, according to Crictracker. This significant turnaround follows Day 2's play on Friday, October 2, at the Sher-i-Kashmir Stadium in Srinagar, where Rest of India had trailed Jammu and Kashmir by 17 runs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/irani-cup-2026-rest-of-india-lead-by-265-runs-after-day-3.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Jammu and Kashmir's first innings saw strong batting performances that powered their resurgence on Day 2. Captain Paras Dogra notably led from the front, scoring a crucial 75 runs off 143 balls, an innings that included six fours and one six. Dogra shared a vital 101-run partnership with Abdul Samad, who contributed a valuable 57 runs, helping J&amp;K build a strong platform and add important runs to their total. Towards the latter stages of the innings, Lone Nasir Muzaffar continued this momentum with an impressive 64, providing further stability as J&amp;K looked to strengthen their position in the contest.</p><p>Rest of India's bowling attack, however, made significant inroads throughout Day 2, spearheaded by left-arm pacer Mukesh Choudhary. Choudhary produced an impressive performance against the hosts, making the most of the conditions with his movement and swing to claim a superb five-wicket haul, finishing with figures of 5/78. He successfully dismissed key batsmen including Qamran Iqbal, Shubham Pundir, Shubham Khajuria, the captain Paras Dogra, and Kanhaiya Wadhawan, effectively putting the opposition under pressure. Choudhary received valuable support from Akash Deep, who picked up three wickets for 43 runs, while Mukesh Kumar chipped in with two wickets for 84 runs. This combined effort from the pace attack helped their side make regular breakthroughs and restrict Jammu and Kashmir's batting progress.</p><p>What to watch: The final day of the Irani Cup 2026 as Rest of India aims to convert their substantial lead into a decisive victory against Jammu and Kashmir.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the provided information, accurately reflecting the game status and player statistics from the provided sources.</p>
