     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-03 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mississauga, Toronto, and Vancouver Secure Wins in Canada Super 60</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Day 3 of the Canada Super 60 Season 2 at BC Place saw victories for the Mississauga Masters, Toronto Sixers, and Vancouver Anchors. The Masters edged the Montreal Royal Tigers by two runs, while the Sixers beat White Rock Warriors by five wickets and the Anchors defeated Brampton Blitz by six wickets. Individual performances were highlighted by Sikandar Raza’s 24-ball fifty, Nicholas Pooran’s 40 off 16, and Moeen Ali’s unbeaten 37.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/mississauga-toronto-and-vancouver-secure-wins-in-canada-supe.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the women's fixture, the Vancouver Warriors Women defeated the Vancouver Anchors Women by eight wickets. Sophie Reid led the chase with an unbeaten 37 after Fatima Sana Khan top-scored for the Anchors with 49.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and captures all key details including specific player performances and match outcomes.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/canada-super-60-season-2-day-3-raza-pooran-and-moeen-ali-star-as-mississauga-toronto-and-vancouver-win-0343/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
