     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-03 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rivian Recalls R2 SUV Over Battery Pack Fastener Defect</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Rivian has issued a recall for its R2 SUV due to fasteners on the high-voltage battery pack that may be improperly tightened, potentially causing power loss while driving. The company identified the defect at its Normal, Illinois factory on September 17 and has since reprogrammed its assembly line to prevent future issues.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/rivian-recalls-r2-suv-over-battery-pack-fastener-defect.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Approximately 14 vehicles are estimated to be affected by the recall. Rivian stated it is unaware of any injuries or accidents related to the issue and will repair or replace components as necessary. This marks the second recall for the new SUV model since deliveries began earlier this year.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and reflects all key details provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/02/rivian-issues-r2-recall-for-poorly-tightened-battery-packs/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
