       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-03 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Search Underway for Three Boys Swept Away at Rushikonda Beach</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Three 14-year-old students from Madhurawada are missing after being swept away by strong waves at Rushikonda beach in Visakhapatnam on October 2, 2026. The boys were playing in the water during a holiday outing when the current pulled them into deeper water, prompting their companions to raise an alarm. Local swimmers initially attempted to rescue the youths without success.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-03/search-underway-for-three-boys-swept-away-at-rushikonda-beac.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Emergency response teams, including marine police, community guards, and a specialized scuba-diving team, have launched an extensive search operation. Commissioner of Police Shankhabrata Bagchi is personally monitoring the efforts at the scene as authorities continue to search the coastal area for the missing boys.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is accurate and adheres to the source material while maintaining an appropriate news-brief tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Visakhapatnam/three-boys-swept-away-at-visakhapatnams-rushikonda-beach-search-on/article71536893.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
